    id: "landmark-thomas-chess", title: "Thomas and Chess: the New York Longitudinal Study of temperament", domain: "development",
    story: "From 1956 Alexander Thomas and Stella Chess followed over a hundred children from infancy into adulthood, rating them on traits such as activity, regularity, mood and adaptability. They described three main types: easy (about 40 per cent), difficult (about 10 per cent) and slow to warm up (about 15 per cent); the rest were mixed.",
