    story: "In 1968 Robert Rosenthal and Lenore Jacobson told teachers at a California primary school that certain pupils, picked at random, were about to 'bloom' intellectually. At the end of the year, some of these pupils, especially in the youngest classes, had gained more on IQ tests than others.",
    believedThen: "That teachers' expectations did not affect pupils' actual performance.",
