    story: "In 1971 Henri Tajfel divided Bristol schoolboys into groups on trivial grounds, such as whether they preferred paintings by Klee or Kandinsky. The boys did not meet group members. When asked to share points, they favoured their own group, even choosing outcomes that maximised the difference between groups over outcomes that gave their own group more.",
