    story: "In the 1950s George Brown noticed that men with schizophrenia discharged from London hospitals relapsed more often if they went to live with parents or wives than with siblings or in lodgings. With John Wing and others he measured 'expressed emotion' in relatives: critical comments, hostility and emotional over-involvement. Vaughn and Leff in 1976 confirmed that high expressed emotion predicted relapse.",
